WEBVTT

00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:13,890
Outside of the metastasis question, would blood tests be recommended?

00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:20,930
Absolutely. So doing blood tests to, so what kind of blood tests should be done on a regular

00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:30,050
basis? A CBC, which will measure red blood cell count, make sure you don't have any type of

00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:39,810
ademia going on will be really good. A complete metabolic panel, so complete metabolic panel would

00:00:39,810 --> 00:00:45,250
measure like your liver function tests, make sure that everything's working well there.

00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:54,050
That those are your two most common things to do as far as blood tests go. And then if you want to

00:00:54,050 --> 00:01:04,130
get into do looking at two remarkers, you are, that's those are more specific tests. But your CBC and

00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:08,370
complete metabolic panel, that'd be the standard thing you'd get done is if you went and got a,

00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:15,730
you know, your your annual checkup, they would do that with a very minimal. If uses two

00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:23,090
remarkers would only be for someone who has a history of cancer. Do Google or Google, sorry, do

00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:30,050
search on that little search bar for two remarkers. And you'll see my blog post about two remarker tests

00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:36,130
to get specific on what two remarkers might be appropriate for you to run, depending on your cancer.

00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:41,730
And then there's other things that you might run. So other blood tests like if you're, you might

00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:50,130
want to get a complete thyroid panel. You might want to get a complete lipid panel. So if you're

00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:56,610
concerned about, you know, your cholesterol balance and triglycerides and things like that,

00:01:56,610 --> 00:02:00,610
those are the other things that you could.

